course: dictionary
lesson: 8785
title: Shameful: judging what people do
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Shameful means so bad or wrong that people should feel ashamed of it. The feeling is shame, but shameful is about the thing that was done. «That is an old idea, that it is shameful for a man to be told what to do by women.» The author says the idea itself is wrong and deserves to be judged harshly.
explain: Use the words around shameful to work out its meaning. In «Even in Britain at the time, many people, like the young William Gladstone, called the war shameful», people are saying the war was so bad that it should be judged with shame. Ask yourself what word would fit: disgraceful? Then swap it in and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Shameful is used for actions: shameful behaviour, a shameful secret, a shameful decision. Notice the phrase «it's shameful that», which tells you the speaker thinks something was wrong. When you meet shameful, ask who did what, and whether it was wrong.
fact: Shameful means causing shame, so bad or wrong that people should feel ashamed of it.
fact: Shameful also means disgraceful, shocking in a bad way.
fact: Shameful is an adjective, and its adverb is shamefully.
fact: Common phrases: «shameful behaviour», «a shameful secret», «it's shameful that».
fact: Shameful judges an action, not just how someone feels.
exercise: «That is an old idea, that it is shameful for a man to be told what to do by women.» What does shameful mean here? | *So wrong that people should feel ashamed of it | Loud and noisy | Very small and tiny | Funny and light-hearted
exercise: «Many people called the war shameful.» Which word is closest in meaning to shameful? | *disgraceful | ordinary | sleepy | cheerful
exercise: Lily says, «It's shameful that he cheated.» What is she judging? | How tall he is | A happy surprise | *Something he did, which was wrong | The colour of his shoes
test: Which word is the adverb of shameful? | *shamefully | shameless | shaming | shameful
test: Mia told a lie to get her friend into trouble. What does shameful suggest about her action? | Something that is very cold | Something she found in the park | *Something so wrong that Mia should feel ashamed | Something that makes Mia laugh
exam: Which sentence uses shameful correctly? | *It is shameful to steal from a friend | The sky was shameful and blue | She ran shameful across the field | Shameful is a colour of paint
